{"track":"est2","num":"2.01","slug":"functions-composite-inverse-logarithmic","title":"Functions: Composite, Inverse & Logarithmic","subtitle":"ClipSAT Printable Practice Suite (clipsat.org) • Topic 2.01 • 20 FRQs + 25 MCQs • Difficulty Progression • Cross-Lesson Synthesis","sections":[{"heading":"Part I — Free-Response Questions (FRQs): Foundational Fluency (1–7)","questions":[{"q":"Find the domain of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x^2-9}$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Domain and range","answer":"The denominator is zero when $x=\\pm3$. Domain: all real $x$ except $x=3$ and $x=-3$.","explanation":"The denominator is zero when $x=\\pm3$. Domain: all real $x$ except $x=3$ and $x=-3$."},{"q":"Find the domain of $g(x)=\\sqrt{7-2x}$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Domain and range","answer":"The radicand must be non-negative: $7-2x\\geq0\\Rightarrow x\\leq\\frac{7}{2}$.","explanation":"The radicand must be non-negative: $7-2x\\geq0\\Rightarrow x\\leq\\frac{7}{2}$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["2**(0.6*x)","log(x + 3) + 0.5"],"xmin":-2.5,"xmax":4.5,"ymin":-2,"ymax":6.5,"asymptotes":{"x":[-3],"y":[0]},"point_labels":[{"x":0,"y":1,"label":"$(0,1)$"}],"width":230}},{"q":"Find the range of $f(x)=-(x-2)^2+5$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Domain and range","answer":"Since $-(x-2)^2\\leq0$ for all $x$, $f(x)\\leq5$. Range: $f(x)\\leq5$.","explanation":"Since $-(x-2)^2\\leq0$ for all $x$, $f(x)\\leq5$. Range: $f(x)\\leq5$."},{"q":"Given $f(x)=x^2+1$ and $g(x)=2x-3$, find $(f\\circ g)(x)$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Composite functions","answer":"$f(g(x))=(2x-3)^2+1=4x^2-12x+9+1=4x^2-12x+10$.","explanation":"$f(g(x))=(2x-3)^2+1=4x^2-12x+9+1=4x^2-12x+10$."},{"q":"Given $f(x)=\\sqrt{x+4}$ and $g(x)=x^2-4$, find $(f\\circ g)(x)$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Composite functions","answer":"$f(g(x))=\\sqrt{(x^2-4)+4}=\\sqrt{x^2}=|x|$.","explanation":"$f(g(x))=\\sqrt{(x^2-4)+4}=\\sqrt{x^2}=|x|$."},{"q":"Using the same $f$ and $g$ as the previous question, find $(g\\circ f)(x)$ and state its domain.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Composite functions","answer":"$g(f(x))=\\left(\\sqrt{x+4}\\right)^2-4=(x+4)-4=x$, valid for $x\\geq-4$ (the domain of $f$).","explanation":"$g(f(x))=\\left(\\sqrt{x+4}\\right)^2-4=(x+4)-4=x$, valid for $x\\geq-4$ (the domain of $f$).","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["2**(0.6*x)","log(x + 3) + 0.5"],"xmin":-2.5,"xmax":4.5,"ymin":-2,"ymax":6.5,"asymptotes":{"x":[-3],"y":[0]},"point_labels":[{"x":0,"y":1,"label":"$(0,1)$"}],"width":230}},{"q":"Find $f^{-1}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\frac{2x-5}{3}$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Inverse functions","answer":"$y=\\frac{2x-5}{3}\\Rightarrow3y=2x-5\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{3y+5}{2}$. So $f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3x+5}{2}$.","explanation":"$y=\\frac{2x-5}{3}\\Rightarrow3y=2x-5\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{3y+5}{2}$. So $f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3x+5}{2}$."}]},{"heading":"Part II — Free-Response Questions (FRQs): Intermediate Multi-Step Application (8–14)","questions":[{"q":"Find $f^{-1}(x)$ for $f(x)=x^3+2$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Inverse functions","answer":"$y=x^3+2\\Rightarrow x=\\sqrt[3]{y-2}$. So $f^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x-2}$.","explanation":"$y=x^3+2\\Rightarrow x=\\sqrt[3]{y-2}$. So $f^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x-2}$."},{"q":"Verify that $f(x)=5x+1$ and $g(x)=\\frac{x-1}{5}$ are inverses by showing $f(g(x))=x$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Verifying inverses","answer":"$f(g(x))=5\\left(\\frac{x-1}{5}\\right)+1=(x-1)+1=x$. Confirmed.","explanation":"$f(g(x))=5\\left(\\frac{x-1}{5}\\right)+1=(x-1)+1=x$. Confirmed."},{"q":"Does $f(x)=x^2$ (for all real $x$) have an inverse function? Explain.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Verifying inverses","answer":"No. $f$ is not one-to-one — it fails the horizontal line test, since for example $f(2)=f(-2)=4$. An inverse function only exists if the domain is restricted (e.g. to $x\\geq0$).","explanation":"No. $f$ is not one-to-one — it fails the horizontal line test, since for example $f(2)=f(-2)=4$. An inverse function only exists if the domain is restricted (e.g. to $x\\geq0$).","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["2**(0.6*x)","log(x + 3) + 0.5"],"xmin":-2.5,"xmax":4.5,"ymin":-2,"ymax":6.5,"asymptotes":{"x":[-3],"y":[0]},"point_labels":[{"x":0,"y":1,"label":"$(0,1)$"}],"width":230}},{"q":"Expand $\\log_b\\left(\\frac{x^3y}{z^2}\\right)$ using the laws of logarithms.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Logarithm laws","answer":"$\\log_b\\left(\\frac{x^3y}{z^2}\\right)=3\\log_bx+\\log_by-2\\log_bz$.","explanation":"$\\log_b\\left(\\frac{x^3y}{z^2}\\right)=3\\log_bx+\\log_by-2\\log_bz$."},{"q":"Condense $2\\log_5x+3\\log_5y-\\log_5z$ into a single logarithm.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Logarithm laws","answer":"$2\\log_5x+3\\log_5y-\\log_5z=\\log_5\\left(\\frac{x^2y^3}{z}\\right)$.","explanation":"$2\\log_5x+3\\log_5y-\\log_5z=\\log_5\\left(\\frac{x^2y^3}{z}\\right)$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\log_2 32-\\log_2 4$ without a calculator.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Logarithm laws","answer":"$\\log_2\\left(\\frac{32}{4}\\right)=\\log_2 8=3$.","explanation":"$\\log_2\\left(\\frac{32}{4}\\right)=\\log_2 8=3$."},{"q":"Solve $\\log_4(x^2)=3$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving logarithmic equations","answer":"$x^2=4^3=64\\Rightarrow x=\\pm8$. Both satisfy the domain requirement $x^2>0$. Solutions: $x=8$ or $x=-8$.","explanation":"$x^2=4^3=64\\Rightarrow x=\\pm8$. Both satisfy the domain requirement $x^2>0$. Solutions: $x=8$ or $x=-8$."}]},{"heading":"Part III — Free-Response Questions (FRQs): Challenging & Cross-Lesson Synthesis (15–20)","questions":[{"q":"Solve $\\ln x+\\ln(x-3)=\\ln10$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving logarithmic equations","cross_lesson":"3.01 Sequences, Series & Complex Numbers","answer":"$\\ln\\left[x(x-3)\\right]=\\ln10\\Rightarrow x^2-3x-10=0\\Rightarrow(x-5)(x+2)=0\\Rightarrow x=5$ or $x=-2$. Since $\\ln(x-3)$ requires $x>3$, reject $x=-2$. Solution: $x=5$.","explanation":"$\\ln\\left[x(x-3)\\right]=\\ln10\\Rightarrow x^2-3x-10=0\\Rightarrow(x-5)(x+2)=0\\Rightarrow x=5$ or $x=-2$. Since $\\ln(x-3)$ requires $x>3$, reject $x=-2$. Solution: $x=5$."},{"q":"Solve $e^{2x-1}=20$, giving your answer to three decimal places.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Exponential equations and logs as inverses","cross_lesson":"4.01 Lines, Triangles & Polygons","answer":"$2x-1=\\ln20\\approx2.996\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{1+2.996}{2}\\approx1.998$.","explanation":"$2x-1=\\ln20\\approx2.996\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{1+2.996}{2}\\approx1.998$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["2**(0.6*x)","log(x + 3) + 0.5"],"xmin":-2.5,"xmax":4.5,"ymin":-2,"ymax":6.5,"asymptotes":{"x":[-3],"y":[0]},"point_labels":[{"x":0,"y":1,"label":"$(0,1)$"}],"width":230}},{"q":"The functions $f(x)=\\log_3x$ and $g(x)=3^x$ are inverses. Use this fact to solve $3^x=81$ without a calculator, and state the value of $g(f(16))$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Exponential equations and logs as inverses","cross_lesson":"5.01 Trigonometry","answer":"$81=3^4$, so $x=4$. Since $f$ and $g$ are inverses, $g(f(16))=16$.","explanation":"$81=3^4$, so $x=4$. Since $f$ and $g$ are inverses, $g(f(16))=16$."},{"q":"The graph shows $f(x)=x^2$ (teal) and $g(x)=(x-2)^2+1$ (indigo). Describe the transformation that maps $f$ onto $g$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Transformations of functions","cross_lesson":"6.01 Circles & Coordinate Geometry","answer":"$g$ is $f$ shifted right $2$ units and up $1$ unit — a horizontal translation of $+2$ followed by a vertical translation of $+1$.","explanation":"$g$ is $f$ shifted right $2$ units and up $1$ unit — a horizontal translation of $+2$ followed by a vertical translation of $+1$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["x**2","(x-2)**2+1"],"xmin":-3,"xmax":5,"ymin":-2,"ymax":10,"width":220}},{"q":"If $h(x)=-f(x+3)$ where $f(x)=x^2$, describe the transformations applied to $f$ to obtain $h$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Transformations of functions","cross_lesson":"7.01 Solid Geometry & Similarity","answer":"Shift $f$ left $3$ units (from $x+3$), then reflect the result over the $x$-axis (from the negative sign outside).","explanation":"Shift $f$ left $3$ units (from $x+3$), then reflect the result over the $x$-axis (from the negative sign outside)."},{"q":"This question has three parts. An investment fund grows according to $A(t)=A_0e^{0.045t}$, where $A_0$ is the initial amount (in dollars) and $t$ is time in years. (a) If $A_0=8000$ dollars, find $A(10)$ to the nearest dollar. (b) Find the time $t$, to the nearest tenth of a year, for the investment to double. (c) Solve for $t$ in terms of $A$ and $A_0$ — that is, find the inverse function $t(A)$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"A well-designed word problem: investment growth and doubling time","cross_lesson":"8.01 Statistics & Probability","answer":"(a) $A(10)=8000e^{0.45}\\approx8000(1.5683)\\approx12546$ dollars. (b) Doubling requires $e^{0.045t}=2\\Rightarrow0.045t=\\ln2\\Rightarrow t=\\frac{\\ln2}{0.045}\\approx15.4$ years. (c) From $A=A_0e^{rt}$: $\\frac{A}{A_0}=e^{rt}\\Rightarrow\\ln\\left(\\frac{A}{A_0}\\right)=rt\\Rightarrow t(A)=\\frac{1}{0.045}\\ln\\left(\\frac{A}{A_0}\\right)$.","explanation":"(a) $A(10)=8000e^{0.45}\\approx8000(1.5683)\\approx12546$ dollars. (b) Doubling requires $e^{0.045t}=2\\Rightarrow0.045t=\\ln2\\Rightarrow t=\\frac{\\ln2}{0.045}\\approx15.4$ years. (c) From $A=A_0e^{rt}$: $\\frac{A}{A_0}=e^{rt}\\Rightarrow\\ln\\left(\\frac{A}{A_0}\\right)=rt\\Rightarrow t(A)=\\frac{1}{0.045}\\ln\\left(\\frac{A}{A_0}\\right)$."}]},{"heading":"Part IV — Multiple-Choice Questions (MCQs): Foundational Concept Mastery (21–28)","questions":[{"q":"If $f(x)=-4x+7$ and $g(x)=-2x-5$, find $(f\\circ g)(7)$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Domain and range","choices":["$83$","$85$","$-19$","$81$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$g(7)=-2(7)-5=-19$. $f(-19)=-4(-19)+7=83$.","explanation":"$g(7)=-2(7)-5=-19$. $f(-19)=-4(-19)+7=83$."},{"q":"If $f(x)=x$ and $g(x)=-3x+3$, find $(f\\circ g)(6)$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Composite functions","choices":["$-13$","$-15$","$-12$","$-17$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$g(6)=-3(6)+3=-15$. $f(-15)=-15$.","explanation":"$g(6)=-3(6)+3=-15$. $f(-15)=-15$."},{"q":"If $f(x)=2x-6$ and $g(x)=-3x+1$, find $(f\\circ g)(3)$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Inverse functions","choices":["$-20$","$-22$","$-8$","$-24$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$g(3)=-3(3)+1=-8$. $f(-8)=2(-8)-6=-22$.","explanation":"$g(3)=-3(3)+1=-8$. $f(-8)=2(-8)-6=-22$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["2**(0.6*x)","log(x + 3) + 0.5"],"xmin":-2.5,"xmax":4.5,"ymin":-2,"ymax":6.5,"asymptotes":{"x":[-3],"y":[0]},"point_labels":[{"x":0,"y":1,"label":"$(0,1)$"}],"width":230}},{"q":"If $f(x)=x$ and $g(x)=3x-9$, find $(f\\circ g)(4)$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Verifying inverses","choices":["$6$","$5$","$1$","$3$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$g(4)=3(4)-9=3$. $f(3)=3$.","explanation":"$g(4)=3(4)-9=3$. $f(3)=3$."},{"q":"If $f(x)=x-1$ and $g(x)=2x+4$, find $(f\\circ g)(-4)$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Logarithm laws","choices":["$-3$","$-7$","$-4$","$-5$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$g(-4)=2(-4)+4=-4$. $f(-4)=(-4)-1=-5$.","explanation":"$g(-4)=2(-4)+4=-4$. $f(-4)=(-4)-1=-5$."},{"q":"If $f(x)=4x+8$ and $g(x)=2x-2$, find $(f\\circ g)(-7)$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Solving logarithmic equations","choices":["$-56$","$-16$","$-58$","$-54$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$g(-7)=2(-7)-2=-16$. $f(-16)=4(-16)+8=-56$.","explanation":"$g(-7)=2(-7)-2=-16$. $f(-16)=4(-16)+8=-56$."},{"q":"If $f(x)=-4x+5$ and $g(x)=2x+3$, find $(f\\circ g)(-2)$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Exponential equations and logs as inverses","choices":["$11$","$7$","$-1$","$9$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$g(-2)=2(-2)+3=-1$. $f(-1)=-4(-1)+5=9$.","explanation":"$g(-2)=2(-2)+3=-1$. $f(-1)=-4(-1)+5=9$."},{"q":"Find $f^{-1}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\frac{6x-5}{8}$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Transformations of functions","choices":["$\\frac{6x+5}{8}$","$\\frac{8x+5}{6}$","$\\frac{8x-5}{6}$","$\\frac{6x-5}{8}$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$y=\\frac{6x-5}{8}\\Rightarrow8y=6x-5\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{8y+5}{6}$. So $f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{8x+5}{6}$.","explanation":"$y=\\frac{6x-5}{8}\\Rightarrow8y=6x-5\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{8y+5}{6}$. So $f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{8x+5}{6}$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["2**(0.6*x)","log(x + 3) + 0.5"],"xmin":-2.5,"xmax":4.5,"ymin":-2,"ymax":6.5,"asymptotes":{"x":[-3],"y":[0]},"point_labels":[{"x":0,"y":1,"label":"$(0,1)$"}],"width":230}}]},{"heading":"Part V — Multiple-Choice Questions (MCQs): Intermediate Exam Application (29–37)","questions":[{"q":"Find $f^{-1}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\frac{9x-13}{4}$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"A well-designed word problem: investment growth and doubling time","choices":["$\\frac{9x-13}{4}$","$\\frac{4x-13}{9}$","$\\frac{9x+13}{4}$","$\\frac{4x+13}{9}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$y=\\frac{9x-13}{4}\\Rightarrow4y=9x-13\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{4y+13}{9}$. So $f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{4x+13}{9}$.","explanation":"$y=\\frac{9x-13}{4}\\Rightarrow4y=9x-13\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{4y+13}{9}$. So $f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{4x+13}{9}$."},{"q":"Find $f^{-1}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\frac{5x-14}{3}$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Inverses & Domain Restrictions","choices":["$\\frac{5x-14}{3}$","$\\frac{3x-14}{5}$","$\\frac{3x+14}{5}$","$\\frac{5x+14}{3}$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$y=\\frac{5x-14}{3}\\Rightarrow3y=5x-14\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{3y+14}{5}$. So $f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3x+14}{5}$.","explanation":"$y=\\frac{5x-14}{3}\\Rightarrow3y=5x-14\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{3y+14}{5}$. So $f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3x+14}{5}$."},{"q":"Find $f^{-1}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\frac{7x-15}{4}$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Composition & Decomposition of Functions","choices":["$\\frac{4x+15}{7}$","$\\frac{7x-15}{4}$","$\\frac{7x+15}{4}$","$\\frac{4x-15}{7}$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$y=\\frac{7x-15}{4}\\Rightarrow4y=7x-15\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{4y+15}{7}$. So $f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{4x+15}{7}$.","explanation":"$y=\\frac{7x-15}{4}\\Rightarrow4y=7x-15\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{4y+15}{7}$. So $f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{4x+15}{7}$."},{"q":"Find $f^{-1}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\frac{5x-2}{8}$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Logarithmic Laws & Base Changes","choices":["$\\frac{5x-2}{8}$","$\\frac{8x-2}{5}$","$\\frac{5x+2}{8}$","$\\frac{8x+2}{5}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$y=\\frac{5x-2}{8}\\Rightarrow8y=5x-2\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{8y+2}{5}$. So $f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{8x+2}{5}$.","explanation":"$y=\\frac{5x-2}{8}\\Rightarrow8y=5x-2\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{8y+2}{5}$. So $f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{8x+2}{5}$."},{"q":"Find $f^{-1}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\frac{2x-11}{6}$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Exponential Models & Logarithmic Graphs","choices":["$\\frac{2x-11}{6}$","$\\frac{2x+11}{6}$","$\\frac{6x-11}{2}$","$\\frac{6x+11}{2}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$y=\\frac{2x-11}{6}\\Rightarrow6y=2x-11\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{6y+11}{2}$. So $f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{6x+11}{2}$.","explanation":"$y=\\frac{2x-11}{6}\\Rightarrow6y=2x-11\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{6y+11}{2}$. So $f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{6x+11}{2}$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["2**(0.6*x)","log(x + 3) + 0.5"],"xmin":-2.5,"xmax":4.5,"ymin":-2,"ymax":6.5,"asymptotes":{"x":[-3],"y":[0]},"point_labels":[{"x":0,"y":1,"label":"$(0,1)$"}],"width":230}},{"q":"Find $f^{-1}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\frac{6x-3}{3}$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Domain and range","choices":["$\\frac{6x-3}{3}$","$\\frac{6x+3}{3}$","$\\frac{3x-3}{6}$","$\\frac{3x+3}{6}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$y=\\frac{6x-3}{3}\\Rightarrow3y=6x-3\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{3y+3}{6}$. So $f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3x+3}{6}$.","explanation":"$y=\\frac{6x-3}{3}\\Rightarrow3y=6x-3\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{3y+3}{6}$. So $f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3x+3}{6}$."},{"q":"Solve $\\ln x+\\ln(x-5)=\\ln6$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Composite functions","choices":["$8$","$-1$","$4$","$6$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$\\ln[x(x-5)]=\\ln6\\Rightarrow x(x-5)=6\\Rightarrow x^2-5x-6=0\\Rightarrow(x-6)(x-(-1))=0\\Rightarrow x=6$ (rejecting $x=-1$ since $x>5$ is required).","explanation":"$\\ln[x(x-5)]=\\ln6\\Rightarrow x(x-5)=6\\Rightarrow x^2-5x-6=0\\Rightarrow(x-6)(x-(-1))=0\\Rightarrow x=6$ (rejecting $x=-1$ since $x>5$ is required)."},{"q":"Solve $\\ln x+\\ln(x-6)=\\ln247$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Inverse functions","choices":["$-13$","$17$","$21$","$19$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$\\ln[x(x-6)]=\\ln247\\Rightarrow x(x-6)=247\\Rightarrow x^2-6x-247=0\\Rightarrow(x-19)(x-(-13))=0\\Rightarrow x=19$ (rejecting $x=-13$ since $x>6$ is required).","explanation":"$\\ln[x(x-6)]=\\ln247\\Rightarrow x(x-6)=247\\Rightarrow x^2-6x-247=0\\Rightarrow(x-19)(x-(-13))=0\\Rightarrow x=19$ (rejecting $x=-13$ since $x>6$ is required)."},{"q":"Solve $e^{3x-7}=105$, giving your answer to three decimal places.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Verifying inverses","choices":["$3.385$","$3.885$","$4.885$","$4.385$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$3x-7=\\ln105\\approx4.654\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{7+4.654}{3}\\approx3.885$.","explanation":"$3x-7=\\ln105\\approx4.654\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{7+4.654}{3}\\approx3.885$."}]},{"heading":"Part VI — Multiple-Choice Questions (MCQs): Challenging & Cross-Lesson Synthesis (38–45)","questions":[{"q":"Solve $e^{4x-6}=488$, giving your answer to three decimal places.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Logarithm laws","choices":["$4.048$","$3.548$","$3.048$","$2.548$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$4x-6=\\ln488\\approx6.190\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{6+6.190}{4}\\approx3.048$.","explanation":"$4x-6=\\ln488\\approx6.190\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{6+6.190}{4}\\approx3.048$.","cross_lesson":"6.01 Circles & Coordinate Geometry"},{"q":"Evaluate $\\log_{5} 500-\\log_{5} 4$ without a calculator.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Solving logarithmic equations","choices":["$496$","$3$","$4$","$2$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\log_{5}\\left(\\frac{500}{4}\\right)=\\log_{5}125=3$.","explanation":"$\\log_{5}\\left(\\frac{500}{4}\\right)=\\log_{5}125=3$.","cross_lesson":"7.01 Solid Geometry & Similarity","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["2**(0.6*x)","log(x + 3) + 0.5"],"xmin":-2.5,"xmax":4.5,"ymin":-2,"ymax":6.5,"asymptotes":{"x":[-3],"y":[0]},"point_labels":[{"x":0,"y":1,"label":"$(0,1)$"}],"width":230}},{"q":"Evaluate $\\log_{3} 72-\\log_{3} 8$ without a calculator.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Exponential equations and logs as inverses","choices":["$64$","$2$","$3$","$1$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\log_{3}\\left(\\frac{72}{8}\\right)=\\log_{3}9=2$.","explanation":"$\\log_{3}\\left(\\frac{72}{8}\\right)=\\log_{3}9=2$.","cross_lesson":"8.01 Statistics & Probability"},{"q":"If $f(x) = \\frac{2x - 5}{3x + 1}$, what is the value of $f^{-1}(1)$?","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Inverses & Domain Restrictions","choices":["$-6$","$-5$","$-4$","$-2$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Set $f(x) = 1$: $\\frac{2x - 5}{3x + 1} = 1 \\Rightarrow 2x - 5 = 3x + 1 \\Rightarrow -x = 6 \\Rightarrow x = -6$.","explanation":"Set $f(x) = 1$: $\\frac{2x - 5}{3x + 1} = 1 \\Rightarrow 2x - 5 = 3x + 1 \\Rightarrow -x = 6 \\Rightarrow x = -6$.","cross_lesson":"1.01 Advanced Algebra"},{"q":"Given $f(x) = x^2 - 4x + 7$ defined on the restricted domain $[2, \\infty)$, what is the equation of $f^{-1}(x)$?","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Inverses & Domain Restrictions","choices":["$f^{-1}(x) = 2 + \\sqrt{x - 3}$","$f^{-1}(x) = 2 - \\sqrt{x - 3}$","$f^{-1}(x) = \\sqrt{x - 7} + 2$","$f^{-1}(x) = 2 + \\sqrt{x + 3}$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Complete the square: $y = (x - 2)^2 + 3 \\Rightarrow y - 3 = (x - 2)^2$. For $x \\geq 2$: $x - 2 = \\sqrt{y - 3} \\Rightarrow x = 2 + \\sqrt{y - 3}$. Thus $f^{-1}(x) = 2 + \\sqrt{x - 3}$.","explanation":"Complete the square: $y = (x - 2)^2 + 3 \\Rightarrow y - 3 = (x - 2)^2$. For $x \\geq 2$: $x - 2 = \\sqrt{y - 3} \\Rightarrow x = 2 + \\sqrt{y - 3}$. Thus $f^{-1}(x) = 2 + \\sqrt{x - 3}$.","cross_lesson":"3.01 Sequences, Series & Complex Numbers"},{"q":"If $h(x) = (2x^2 - 1)^5$, identify inner function $g(x)$ and outer function $f(u)$ such that $h(x) = f(g(x))$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Composition & Decomposition of Functions","choices":["$g(x) = 2x^2 - 1$ and $f(u) = u^5$","$g(x) = x^5$ and $f(u) = 2u^2 - 1$","$g(x) = 2x$ and $f(u) = (u - 1)^5$","$g(x) = 2x^2$ and $f(u) = u^5 - 1$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Direct decomposition gives inner $g(x) = 2x^2 - 1$ and outer power function $f(u) = u^5$.","explanation":"Direct decomposition gives inner $g(x) = 2x^2 - 1$ and outer power function $f(u) = u^5$.","cross_lesson":"4.01 Lines, Triangles & Polygons"},{"q":"Using the change of base formula, evaluate $\\log_8(32)$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Logarithmic Laws & Base Changes","choices":["$\\frac{5}{3}$","$\\frac{3}{5}$","$4$","$\\frac{4}{3}$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Express with base $2$: $\\log_8(32) = \\frac{\\log_2 32}{\\log_2 8} = \\frac{5}{3}$.","explanation":"Express with base $2$: $\\log_8(32) = \\frac{\\log_2 32}{\\log_2 8} = \\frac{5}{3}$.","cross_lesson":"5.01 Trigonometry"},{"q":"What is the vertical asymptote of the graph of $f(x) = 3\\ln(2x - 8) + 1$?","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Exponential Models & Logarithmic Graphs","choices":["$x = 4$","$x = 8$","$x = 0$","$y = 1$"],"correct":0,"answer":"The argument of the natural log equals zero at the vertical asymptote: $2x - 8 = 0 \\Rightarrow 2x = 8 \\Rightarrow x = 4$.","explanation":"The argument of the natural log equals zero at the vertical asymptote: $2x - 8 = 0 \\Rightarrow 2x = 8 \\Rightarrow x = 4$.","cross_lesson":"6.01 Circles & Coordinate Geometry"}]}]}